      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Guideline Updates",
      "summary": "Taking up a new version of a guideline, or a changed lower layer, is a re-pin and a review at once.",
      "description": "Taking up a new version of a guideline, or a changed lower layer, is a\nre-pin and a review at once. The steward maps the affected layers and\nre-pins them in dependency order. For each re-pin, the adaptation team\ncompares the old version, the new version and its own adaptations. A\nchange that touches no adaptation or policy merges on the technical\npath. One that does goes to the adaptation committee, which decides for\neach adaptation whether to keep, revise or retire it. Revisions are\nordinary content changes (Process_ContentChangeReview), and the re-pin\nmerges with them. The loop runs until every layer is current.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant-core/blob/main/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn",
